    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "In this paper we are using a BEM algorithm for 3 D modelling of geological structures typical in sedimentary basins with tectonic movement. We outline the basic theory of the BEM. The focus in this paper is on 3d surface unfolding, based on a geo-mechanical approach and given as an alternative to the more common geometrical techniques. We do not treat the rheology of a sedimentary basin, but assume our rock mass to be linear elastic. Simple examples of unfolding and bending are presented. We also present our plans for further development in order to treat an entire sedimentary basin, with arbitrary many faults and fault blocks.",
